{
 "_about": "Essential oil descriptions for the library. Each is a supplier text (Fraterworks product page, cached in vendor/fraterworks) read for odour and mapped to the 138-word GS-LF vocabulary; weights are in the brief mapper's currency, where a weight is read directly as a percept probability. The brief mapper itself (perfumer llm.prose_to_brief) could not run (its API key returned 401), so the maps were written by hand from the same text and vocabulary. Six poorly represented oils (Petitgrain, Lavandin, Vetiver, Lime, Labdanum, Tangerine) were revised from web sources on 2026-11-10; each of their words carries a provenance: 'text' (supplier text), 'revised' (supplier weight changed, old weight kept) or 'web' (added from web sources, listed per oil). Web sources are mostly trade copy and disagree on several points. 'match' says how close the described product is to the composed oil: exact, close, proxy (a sibling origin or grade; only words that hold for the family are kept), heart (a fraction; the whole-oil map is from the web) or none. Every map was re-read against its cached text on 2026-11-10 and each change is listed in that oil's 'review'. scripts/build_naturals.py applies the maps to the composed vectors, raise-only (PERCEPT_EVIDENCE.md, 'Oil descriptions'); 'avoid' is recorded and never applied. The comparison with the composed vector is written to artifacts/naturals.json ('described'), not kept here. Not yet confirmed by the perfumer's nose.",
